# Export a portable learnlog bundle

```tutorial-step
required_patterns:
  - mode: regex
    pattern: 'learnlog\s+export\b[^\n]*(?<!\S)(?:-o|--output)\b\s+\S+\.learnlog\b'
hint: Pick an output name ending in `.learnlog`.
```

Create a portable bundle file with `learnlog export -o course.learnlog`.
This is the easiest format to hand to someone for playback.

# Export a ProgSnap2 dataset

```tutorial-step
required_patterns:
  - mode: regex
    pattern: 'learnlog\s+export\b[^\n]*--progsnap2\b'
  - mode: regex
    pattern: 'learnlog\s+export\b[^\n]*(?<!\S)(?:-o|--output)\b\s+\S+\.progsnap2\b'
hint: Use `--progsnap2` when the goal is analysis rather than playback.
```

Export the same log as a ProgSnap2 zip so it can be used for CS
education analysis workflows.

# Configure a remote repository

```tutorial-step
required_patterns:
  - mode: regex
    pattern: 'learnlog\s+set-remote\s+\S+'
hint: Point `origin` at a Git repository URL or local bare repo path.
```

Choose a remote repository and configure it with
`learnlog set-remote ../course.git`.
For local practice, a bare repository path such as `../course.git`
works well; for sharing across machines, pass a real URL instead.

# Push the log to the remote

```tutorial-step
required_patterns:
  - learnlog push
hint: Push after `set-remote` so the remote receives all branches.
```

Run `learnlog push` to send the whole recorded history to `origin`.

# Clone the log somewhere else

```tutorial-step
required_patterns:
  - mode: regex
    pattern: 'learnlog\s+clone\s+\S+'
hint: Try cloning into a second directory to simulate another machine.
```

In another empty directory, use `learnlog clone <remote>` to retrieve
the shared `.learnlog/` repository.

# Pull later updates

```tutorial-step
required_patterns:
  - learnlog pull
hint: After new commits are pushed, run `learnlog pull` in the clone.
```

When the original project has received more recorded runs and pushed
them, update the clone with `learnlog pull`.
